          "Handling slow overloaded targets cleanly benefits from indirect paths too: sometimes target `B` only dropped `A`'s UDP packet due to a momentary socket buffer spike that clears before `k` relays ping milliseconds later. Direct ping timeouts frequently blame healthy nodes falsely during brief kernel scheduler stalls, overloaded ingress queues, or asymmetric single-pair switch micro-partitions cleanly. Delegating indirect `ping-req` probes across `k` independent healthy relay peers separates true process crashes cleanly from isolated pairwise packet loss between observer and target cleanly. Requiring unanimous timeout across direct plus indirect relay paths slashes false-positive eviction storms dramatically while keeping detection latency sub-second across production racks. Indirect `ping-req` relays route around asymmetric switch blackholes cleanly by testing connectivity from multiple independent third-party cluster angles safely. Distinguishing true kernel panics from local packet drops dramatically curtails destructive unnecessary shard leadership handoffs and state rebalancing storms cleanly. Relay timeouts fit comfortably inside protocol period deadlines without delaying real crash alerts. Indirect `ping-req` verification routes probe checks through `k` healthy third-party relays whenever direct UDP sockets time out intermittently across noisy switches cleanly. Distinguishing isolated asymmetric route flaps from genuine server panics saves storage teams from pointless emergency partition rebalances cleanly.",
