          "Reading `phi` on a base-10 log scale delivers intuitive probability orders of magnitude: `phi = 1.0` equals a `10%` false-suspicion chance, `phi = 2.0` equals `1%`, `phi = 3.0` equals `0.1%`, and `phi = 8.0` represents a one-in-100-million anomaly.",
