          "Examine our unified coordinator architecture clearly: clients initiate `SagaStart`, Orchestrator writes commands into its durable state log + Outbox, CDC delivers commands reliably to worker services, workers commit domain + dedup + reply atomically, and CDC returns replies to drive the next transition or reverse LIFO compensation.",
          "Milestone 9 brings Days 42 through 44 together by eliminating the brittle dual-write vulnerability inherent inside naive saga orchestrators. Even a durable orchestrator fails silently if it commits local saga state (`T2_PENDING`) to SQL and then crashes before publishing the `T2` command over a message bus—or publishes `T2` first and crashes before updating SQL. `OutboxSagaWorker` resolves this exact boundary by embedding saga state transitions and outgoing command messages inside a single atomic database transaction.",
