          "Think critically about three production failure edge cases in hinted handoff that wreck naive clusters if left unguarded:",
          "First, **Hint Expiration (`max_hint_window`, e.g. 3 hours)**: if `NodeB` died permanently with a fried motherboard for four days, buffering gigabytes of hints indefinitely on `NodeD` would fill `NodeD`'s SSD and cascade crash healthy `NodeD` too! Hints older than `max_hint_window` MUST drop cleanly, leaving full recovery to anti-entropy repair or node rebuild.",
