          "Accepting writes onto temporary standby nodes during a sloppy-quorum outage leaves primary replicas stale once the downed node boots back online or the partition heals. **Hinted Handoff** completes the availability loop by shipping buffered fallback records back to their rightful owners asynchronously. `HintedStandby` models both temporary hint queuing (`store_hint`) and safe bounded drain (`drain_to_recovered`) when primary targets return.",
          "Examine `HintedStandby.store_hint` alongside its crucial `max_window_ms` parameter: hinted handoff cannot safely buffer arbitrary weeks of traffic without threatening standby node disks! If a primary replica dies permanently (e.g., fried motherboard never replaced for days), queuing unlimited hints on neighboring nodes slowly fills standby SSDs until cascading disk-full outages take down healthy nodes too. Enforcing `max_window_ms` sheds stale hints once outages cross configured time caps.",
