          "Recognizing Hinted Handoff's strict durability limitation prevents over-reliance on hints alone as an anti-entropy mechanism. What happens if the standby node holding hints crashes permanently *after* `max_window_ms` expires hints, or loses disk data before draining? Hints merely accelerate short outage convergence; they NEVER replace periodic background **Merkle-tree anti-entropy repair** (`nodetool repair`), which remains essential for permanent consistency.",
