          "Production systems support three distinct resolution tiers depending on semantics: **Last-Write-Wins (HLC tie-broken)** for idempotent independent metadata like `last_login_ip`; **CRDT Data Types** (`OR-Set` for shopping carts, `PN-Counter` for inventory/likes) that merge algebraically inside storage with zero siblings exposed externally; and **Application-Level Semantic Mergers** returning siblings cleanly when human/business choice is mandatory.",
          "Amazon's Dynamo paper illustrated a famous shopping-cart anomaly showing why `OR-Set / union merge` semantics beat simple LWW for carts:",
