          "Analyze the concurrent add-vs-remove race to verify **Add-Wins** convergence cleanly: both Replica A and Replica B observe `'milk'` tagged `t1`. Replica A executes `remove(`'milk'`)`, adding `t1` to `A.removes`. Concurrently, Replica B executes `add(`'milk'`)` freshly, minting brand-new unique tag `t2` in `B.adds`. After merging `A` and `B`, `t1` stays masked inside `removes`, yet `t2` survives intact—reflecting the user's latest concurrent re-addition without accidentally deleting new intent, while an earlier delete still erases `t1` cleanly!",
