          "Compute average cluster load per node (`avg = ceil((1 + epsilon) * total_active_load / N)` where `epsilon` is a configurable slack factor like `0.25`, setting hard cap `1.25x` average!).",
          "When hashing incoming key `K`, locate primary ring owner `node = ring_next(hash(K))`. Check whether `current_load[node] < max_cap`: if under cap, serve straight on `node`! If `node` hit its `1.25 * avg` cap, simply **walk clockwise along the ring** to the next node whose load stays below `max_cap`!",
