          "Examine `BoundedHashRing` (`pick_node`) implementing Google's **Consistent Hashing with Bounded Loads** (Mirrokni, Thorup & Zadimoghaddam, 2016 — used in Vimeo, HAProxy, and Google Maglev/load-balancers). On a classical hash ring, one viral key (`taylor_swift_livestream` or `sale_sku_1`) hits a single home shard endlessly while adjacent ring neighbors sit completely idle! `BoundedHashRing` assigns every active node an explicit **capacity ceiling (`ceil(c * total_load / num_nodes)` where load factor `c >= 1.25`)**.",
