          "Distinguishing **passive request telemetry (`error rate`, `RTT`)** from **active periodic health probes (`/healthz`)** prevents blind spots on low-QPS shards as well as false alarms on noisy peers. Active probes detect dead sockets even during low traffic, yet can return healthy `200 OK` while user-data database queries deadlock! Combining passive traffic errors (`5xx` / timeout rate on real queries) with lightweight heartbeats gives accurate real-world visibility.",
          "Telemetry smoothing using EWMA latency updates prevents one single anomalous client timeout from tripping `ShardHealthTelemetry` unnecessarily across thousands of healthy requests. Similarly, capping per-shard `inflight` inside telemetry connects Day 52 concurrency bounding directly with Day 54 ring routing—steering spillover naturally onto cooler ring neighbors *before* queues spiral.",
