          "When a barrier arrives on any channel, the operator immediately persists its current state, captures all unconsumed records sitting ahead of the barrier in channel buffers, and passes the barrier downstream without blocking any input channel.",
          "Additionally, transactional two-phase commit (2PC) sinks allow external relational databases and object stores to participate in exactly-once output: records are written into pre-committed transaction handles, and committed only when the coordinator broadcasts global checkpoint success.",
