          "Notice the **cascading failure trap** if `TailBasedSampler` keeps 100% of error traces during a massive regional outage when 50% of all cluster traffic suddenly errors out! Instead of saving 1% of traces, keeping 100% of errors during a 50% outage spikes collector ingest by `50x`—crashing the observability cluster right when SREs depend on trace graphs to stop the bleeding! Pairing tail rules with strict per-second **rate-limited error caps** prevents observability meltdowns cleanly.",
          "Hybrid **Head + Tail Sampling** optimizes massive hyper-scale pipelines (`>1M QPS`): heads drop obviously uninformative baseline health-check traffic early, or pass ~10% candidate flows (plus forced debug tenants) forward into tail collectors that filter sharply down to errors, tail anomalies, and 1% baseline cohorts.",
