          "Analyze `SpanNode` and `compute_critical_path(spans)` carefully to formalize **Critical Path Analysis** (inspired by Google Dapper & Uber CRISP): starting from the root span's `end_ms` and walking backward along causal execution (`parent_span_id`, `start_ms`, `end_ms`), the critical path consists strictly of the chain of non-overlapping execution intervals whose delays directly forced the parent/root span to wait! Any time spent inside an ancestor when no blocking child ran counts as **self-time (`local work`)**, while blocking child intervals propagate the path straight to whichever child finished latest (`blocking edge`)!",
