          "Notice carefully the common pitfall separating **async fire-and-forget spans (`detached`)** from **blocking awaited spans (`join`)**! If Root emits an asynchronous Kafka notification at `t = 15 ms` and immediately returns HTTP `200 OK` at `t = 20 ms`, while the background consumer finishes at `t = 500 ms` (`child.end_ms > parent.end_ms`), treating that un-awaited consumer naively as blocking Root's end time corrupts critical-path calculations completely! Checking containment (`child_end <= parent_end` or explicit async link flags) isolates true synchronous user-latency paths from background async work.",
          "Decomposing total critical-path duration by **service / team ownership** yields crisp executive optimization roadmaps: instead of debating hunches across twenty microservice teams, critical-path attribution computes exact percentages (`Auth: 12%`, `DB Shard Lock: 58%`, `Serialization self-time: 18%`, `Network gap: 12%`) across thousands of slow `p99` tail traces automatically!",
